PITR restored the base backup and replayed the WAL up to the named restore point created just before the mistake, recovering all 57,000 orders, RPO 0, in 335 ms.

477
00:31:33.339 --> 00:31:43.046
Without WAL archiving you could only restore the base backup (losing everything since it); without a recorded safe point you'd be guessing where to stop replay.

478
00:31:43.326 --> 00:31:50.281
The named restore point (what a deploy or ops tool creates before a risky operation) makes the target exact.

