00:33:20.911 --> 00:33:30.041
ASYNC replication lag = the RPO window (committed but not yet streamed) ==. peak replication lag during the burst:

499
00:33:30.321 --> 00:33:49.137
16376 KB of un-replayed WAL on the standby. - if the primary is lost at that instant, that un-streamed WAL is the async RPO (a. small window of commits). after the burst drains, lag settles to 0 bytes (standby caught up).

500
00:33:49.417 --> 00:33:50.185
