00:34:41.527 --> 00:34:59.425
Synchronous replication (synchronousstandbynames) made every commit wait for the standby to persist the WAL, so after killing the primary the standby had every committed row, RPO 0, at the cost of commit latency and the availability risk that a lost standby blocks commits.

